# Set the default behavior, in case people don't have core.autocrlf set.
* text eol=lf

# Denote all files that are truly binary and should not be modified.
*.sig binary
*.png binary
# Without this the `* text eol=lf` above normalises the PKCS#12 keystore on
# commit, stripping its CR bytes: the file lands in the repository corrupt and
# the eudi_openid4vp containers die at startup with java.io.EOFException.
*.p12 binary
testdata/storage_regression/**/bbolt_client_db binary
testdata/storage_regression/**/eudi_client_db binary
# CBOR test vectors are raw bytes, and 0x0D appears in them constantly -- a CBOR
# head byte, a length, a string byte. Under the `* text eol=lf` default above
# they are normalised on commit exactly as the PKCS#12 keystore was, and land in
# the repository corrupt: `cbor: invalid UTF-8 string` on a vector that parses
# perfectly in the working tree, because the working copy was never re-checked
# out. Found on PR #735 by a reviewer who cloned and ran the tests.
*.cbor binary

# Same hazard, not yet triggered: a DER certificate is raw bytes too.
*.der binary
